  "name": "Trauma Recovery Measure (TRM)",
  "short_name": null,
  "language": "en",
  "description": "The Trauma Recovery Measure (TRM) is a 15-item self-report questionnaire developed to measure psychological recovery following exposure to trauma in adult populations (ages 18+). Trauma recovery has been defined as an individual process of cognitive change, leading to enhanced emotional and behavioural control and the attainment of intrapersonal mastery, empowerment, and hope for oneself and the future (Smith, 2022).",
